scion: a cache of translated code (backend/x64/a64_code_cache.cpp), shared by the JITs of a process and kept on disk
for the next process: a block that has been compiled is copied into a JIT's code and relocated instead of being
compiled again, as long as the guest instructions there are the same. Needs patches/xbyak-reloc-hook.patch.
- after a block is emitted, the fields that refer outside it are recorded symbolically: rel32 and rip-relative
  references to prelude code, constants, fastmem fallbacks and the host executable, and mov immediates that are the
  JIT's own pointers (configuration, callbacks, tpidr registers, exclusive monitor slots); block links are emitted
  again by the JIT that installs the copy, fastmem fault information is relocated with it
- UserConfig::code_cache (MakeCodeCache), with code_cache_verify (also decode each block with Zydis and compare, and
  compile cached blocks again and compare) and code_cache_selftest (run every block from a relocated copy) for testing
- LoadCodeCache / SaveCodeCache: a file of checksummed records, tied to a key (the build of the host) and to the
  JITs' configuration, mapped and read lazily (a record is parsed when its location is first looked for); a few new
  blocks are appended, more rewrite the file with what other processes saved meanwhile, dropping the records no
  process has looked for in 8 rewrites

