+/* This file is part of the dynarmic project.
+ * SPDX-License-Identifier: 0BSD
+ */
+
+/* Code cache: a block one JIT has compiled is copied into the code of other JITs (other guest threads) instead of being
+ * compiled again. Each JIT keeps its own code buffer, so nothing changes for code that runs, links or is invalidated
+ * concurrently: only the cache's map is shared.
+ *
+ * After a block is emitted it is captured: every field of it that refers to something outside the block is recorded in
+ * a form another JIT can resolve. Xbyak reports those fields as it emits them (relocHook_): rel32 operands and
+ * rip-relative addresses, which point to prelude code, constants, fastmem fallbacks or the host executable, and the
+ * immediates of mov reg, imm, some of which are this JIT's pointers (its configuration, callbacks, tpidr registers,
+ * exclusive monitor slots). Block links (patch locations) are emitted again by the JIT that installs the copy. A block
+ * that refers to anything else (another block, an unknown address in the code buffer) is not cached.
+ * code_cache_verify checks the fields Xbyak reported against the ones found by decoding the block (Zydis), and each
+ * copy against the block compiled again. */
+
